      "role": "user",
      "content": "i spent forty years studying the intricacies of philology, thinking there was something sacred about the way language shapes the human soul. now i sit in this office and watch these machines churn out perfect syntax in seconds. it feels like i've spent my whole life building a cathedral only to find out the world has moved on to digital ghosts. there's no use in continuing to study something that has been solved by an algorithm. it just feels like i'm taking up space in a world that doesn't need me anymore.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
